text:
emily: Quick check — hitting a customer-facing error that only reproduces in prod. I need to capture request+response pairs for ~1 hour to debug. They include prompt text and some headers (maybe tokens). Can security sign off on a timeboxed capture?

raj: What’s the absolute minimum we need to capture? full bodies or samples? we can do timeboxed access but prefer sampled and redacted.

emily: Ideally 100–200 request/response pairs around the error window. If we can mask Authorization and any token-like headers before write, and hash the prompt field, that should be fine.

nina: Heads up: policy forbids storing raw auth tokens or un-hashed secrets. We can approve a temporary capture if you follow controls: sample only, remove/mask Authorization+Cookie+any X-API-Token headers, hash prompt/personal fields, store in an access-controlled bucket, retention <=24h, and log the approval in a ticket.

olivia: Can we implement hashing in the proxy layer? Example: HMAC-SHA256 with a per-environment key and only store hex digest + length. Keeps debugging signal without raw text.

raj: Yep — will add a middleware to: strip/mask these headers, compute hmac for prompt and username, and write to /tmp/secure-logs bucket with lifecycle 1d. Will also set AWS KMS key for the HMAC secret.

nina: Please include the scrub regex & test vectors in the PR. Also add an automated check that drops any value matching token regex (e.g., /Bearer\s+[A-Za-z0-9\-\._~\+\/]+=*/). If you accidentally capture a token, rotate it immediately and tell security.

emily: Copy. Filing ticket with scope and retention: https://redwood.atlassian.net/browse/ENG-12345 — will attach sample sanitized output.

olivia: Quick middleware snippet I'll use (Node/Express):

```
// sanitize middleware
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  const scrubHeader = h => req.headers[h] && '[REDACTED]';
  if (req.headers.authorization) req.headers.authorization = '[REDACTED]';
  if (req.headers.cookie) req.headers.cookie = '[REDACTED]';
  // HMAC prompt
  if (req.body && req.body.prompt) {
    req.body._prompt_hash = hmacHex(process.env.HMAC_KEY, req.body.prompt);
    delete req.body.prompt;
  }
  next();
});
```

raj: I'll open a small PR and route it to a feature branch. deploy-bot: can you schedule a short canary run when PR merges?

deploy-bot: deploy scheduled: canary to staging -> prod canary window 30m after merge. :white_check_mark:

nina: Approved conditionally — security approves the capture for 24h starting when the canary is live. Requirements: PR linked to ticket, KMS key control, retention tag set. I’ll post the approval ID in the ticket.

emily: Thanks all — will implement and ping when live. cc @raj for followups. :thumbsup:

raj: Follow-up: once we have samples, I’ll export only the hashed prompt + status codes + timing. No raw body will be left in long-term storage.

olivia: Added unit tests for scrub and regex. Will include test vectors.

nina: Great — closing here pending PR link in the ticket. Remember: rotate any leaked tokens and notify sec immediately.
